Parse the CSS animation shorthand grammar: a keyword fills the first longhand
it is valid for that is still unset (easing, iteration count, direction, fill
mode, play state), else names the animation, and a name of none runs nothing.
Add the reverse and alternate-reverse directions and the backwards, forwards
and both fill modes: a backwards fill holds the first frame during the delay, a
forwards fill keeps the final frame until the animation is removed. Fractional
or zero iteration counts and paused animations are rejected, not rounded or
dropped.

